      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "If $\\text{Var}[X]=100,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[3-0.2X].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+b]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-0.2$ and $b=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3-0.2X] & ={(-0.2)}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =0.04\\cdot 100 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
